& [PublicAPIBoundary: IR7OperationsDryRunSimulator] is the future public API boundary for IR7 implementation
  + [api] is validate_operation_request(envelope, authority_basis, policy) returns accepted operation_request_projection or refusal
  + [api] is classify_intended_effect_and_target(request, policy) returns dry_run_allowed, review_required, refusal, or SOP-first interrupt
  + [api] is build_dry_run_result(request, simulated_context, policy) returns dry_run_result with live_effect_performed false
  + [api] is classify_resource_safety(request, dry_run_result, policy) returns resource_safety_review, human_review_required, refusal, or interrupt
  + [api] is review_human_approval(approval_record, operation_request, policy) returns fresh_scoped, stale, revoked, mismatched, broad_invalid, or refusal
  + [api] is classify_operation_action(action_packet, policy) returns route, refusal, or SOP-first interrupt context
  + [api] is validate_generated_operations_output_path(path, generated_output_policy) returns accepted generated path or refusal
  + [api] is run_operations_dry_run_fixture(fixture_case, expected_ledger, runner_policy) returns generated fixture comparison report
  + [api_status] is future implementation target only

  = must: make authority tier, freshness, intended effect, resource target, risk, blast radius, credential boundary, network boundary, approval state, rollback route, refusal reason, and live_effect_performed visible in return values
  = must: avoid APIs named or shaped as command executor, process starter, GPU scheduler, model runtime controller, job dispatcher, secret reader, network opener, destructive filesystem actor, persistent automation runner, operations controller, or live machine controller

