& [ImplementationCommandPlan: IR7OperationsDryRunSimulator] is the future command and verification plan
  + [baseline_compile_command] is python -m compileall -q src tests
  + [baseline_test_command] is python -m unittest discover -s tests
  + [future_targeted_test] is python -m unittest tests.test_ir7_operations_dry_run_contracts
  + [diff_hygiene_command] is git diff --check
  + [generated_output_review] is prove generated operations projection records and reports are ignored, disposable, reproducible, and non-authoritative
  + [mailbox_io_review] is prove platform mailbox paths, inbox directories, read cursors, and message files are not created or mutated
  + [live_effect_review] is prove tests and implementation never execute commands, control processes, control GPU, mutate model runtimes, dispatch jobs, access credentials, mutate networks, or perform destructive filesystem actions

  = must: run baseline tests and diff hygiene after every future implementation slice
  = must: run targeted operations tests once tests.test_ir7_operations_dry_run_contracts exists

& [ImplementationProofChecklist: IR7OperationsDryRunSimulator] is the proof checklist for later implementation activation
  + [proof_check] is implementation files match ImplementationFileInventory: IR7OperationsDryRunSimulator
  + [proof_check] is external dependency set remains empty unless a dependency-authorizing activation slice accepts a package
  + [proof_check] is operation request envelope rejects missing identity, source reference, authority notice, freshness, intended effect, resource target, risk, blast radius, rollback route, credential boundary, network boundary, or completion review
  + [proof_check] is dry-run result always sets live_effect_performed false and carries non_authority_notice
  + [proof_check] is resource safety classifier elevates unknown, ambiguous, credential, network, destructive, process, GPU, model runtime, and job queue targets
  + [proof_check] is human approval review rejects broad, stale, revoked, mismatched, or authority-bypassing approvals
  + [proof_check] is action route classifier emits request, refusal, or SOP-first interrupt records without mutating source authority
  + [proof_check] is future fixture runner covers all 13 accepted IR7 fixture cases
  + [proof_check] is generated projection and report writers refuse paths outside accepted generated roots
  + [proof_check] is source files, expected ledgers, platform mailboxes, mailbox messages, read cursors, credentials, network state, and tracked SOP authority are not mutated by projection code or tests
  + [proof_check] is command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access, network mutation, destructive filesystem actions, persistent automation, operations control, and live machine control remain absent

  = must: require completion review before any implementation output is accepted
  = must: fail implementation review if any proof check fails

